event: message
data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"content":[{"text":"[{\"name\":\"boc_get_group\",\"description\":\"Get a Bank of Canada Valet group's description and member series.\\n\\nUse for: discovering all the series in a themed group before\\nfetching their observations together, e.g. FX_RATES_DAILY (daily\\nexchange rates for ~27 currencies) or CPI_MONTHLY (Total CPI plus\\ncore-inflation measures such as CPI-trim, CPI-median, CPI-common).\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"lang\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"fr\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"name\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"name\":\"bis_compare_countries\",\"description\":\"Compare Canada with G7 or other economies on a BIS financial indicator.\\n\\nUse for: how Canada's household debt service ratio, credit-to-GDP gap,\\nhousehold or government debt as a share of GDP, real house price\\ngrowth, policy rate, inflation or effective exchange rate compares\\nwith the United States, the United Kingdom, Australia, the euro area\\nor the G7. `indicator` is one of the preset names; Canada is always\\nfirst. `compare_with` takes \\\"G7\\\", \\\"EURO_AREA\\\" or two-letter BIS area\\ncodes (\\\"US\\\", \\\"GB\\\", \\\"AU\\\", \\\"NZ\\\", \\\"SE\\\", \\\"NO\\\"). Periods are SDMX\\n(`2020`, `2020-Q1`, `2020-01`); without them the last 5 years come\\nback. The result gives Canada's rank (1 = highest) in the period most\\nof them report. Bank of Canada Valet and StatCan are better for\\nCanada's own latest figures.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"indicator\":{\"enum\":[\"policy_rate\",\"household_debt_service_ratio\",\"private_debt_service_ratio\",\"credit_to_gdp_gap\",\"household_credit_to_gdp\",\"private_credit_to_gdp\",\"government_debt_to_gdp\",\"real_house_price_growth\",\"nominal_house_price_growth\",\"real_house_price_index\",\"cpi_inflation\",\"real_effective_exchange_rate\",\"nominal_effective_exchange_rate\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"compare_with\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"start_period\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"end_period\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"last_n\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"lang\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"fr\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"indicator\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"name\":\"boc_search_groups\",\"description\":\"Search or list Bank of Canada Valet's series groups (~2,500).\\n\\nUse for: finding a themed group of related series (e.g. daily\\nexchange rates, the CPI family including CPI-trim/median/common,\\nweekly/monthly/annual commodity price indexes) when you want several\\nrelated series at once rather than one series name. Pass `query`\\nfor a keyword search (top `limit` matches, default 25, max 200). Omit\\n`query` to page through the groups (`limit` default 50, max 1000).\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"limit\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"lang\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"fr\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"name\":\"boc_get_series\",\"description\":\"Get the label, description and status of one Bank of Canada Valet series.\\n\\nUse for: confirming what a series code actually measures before\\nrequesting its observations, e.g. FXUSDCAD (USD/CAD daily exchange\\nrate), V39079 (target for the overnight rate / policy rate),\\nV80691311 (prime rate), V41690973 (Total CPI). Also says whether it\\nis still updated: `status` discontinued when its newest observation\\n(`last_observation`) is far older than its frequency allows, with the\\n`successor` where the Bank replaced it (the noon rate IEXE0101, last\\n2017-04-28, by the daily average FXUSDCAD), and a `note` on FX* rates\\n(indicative daily averages by about 16:30 ET, not transactional).\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"lang\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"fr\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"name\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"name\":\"boc_search_series\",\"description\":\"Search or list Bank of Canada Valet's ~16,000 statistical series.\\n\\nUse for: finding a Valet series name when you only know a topic -\\nexchange rates, interest rates (policy rate, prime rate), CPI/\\ninflation measures, commodity prices, and hundreds of other\\nmonetary/financial series. Pass `query` for a keyword search (top\\n`limit` matches, default 25, max 200). Omit `query` to page through\\nthe catalogue in name order (`limit` default 50, max 1000);\\n`total_count` is the full number and provenance.limits says what was\\ncut. Legacy series are listed too, each with `status`\\n(active/discontinued, from its newest observation against its\\nfrequency), `last_observation` and, where known, `successor`: e.g.\\nthe noon rate IEXE0101 ended 2017-04-28, replaced by the daily\\naverage FXUSDCAD. FX* rates carry a `note`: indicative daily\\naverages published by about 16:30 ET, not transactional rates.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"limit\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"integer\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}],\"default\":null},\"lang\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"fr\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}]","type":"text"}],"isError":false,"structuredContent":{"result":[{"name":"boc_get_group","description":"Get a Bank of Canada Valet group's description and member series.\n\nUse for: discovering all the series in a themed group before\nfetching their observations together, e.g. FX_RATES_DAILY (daily\nexchange rates for ~27 currencies) or CPI_MONTHLY (Total CPI plus\ncore-inflation measures such as CPI-trim, CPI-median, CPI-common).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"lang":{"default":"en","enum":["en","fr"],"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"bis_compare_countries","description":"Compare Canada with G7 or other economies on a BIS financial indicator.\n\nUse for: how Canada's household debt service ratio, credit-to-GDP gap,\nhousehold or government debt as a share of GDP, real house price\ngrowth, policy rate, inflation or effective exchange rate compares\nwith the United States, the United Kingdom, Australia, the euro area\nor the G7. `indicator` is one of the preset names; Canada is always\nfirst. `compare_with` takes \"G7\", \"EURO_AREA\" or two-letter BIS area\ncodes (\"US\", \"GB\", \"AU\", \"NZ\", \"SE\", \"NO\"). Periods are SDMX\n(`2020`, `2020-Q1`, `2020-01`); without them the last 5 years come\nback. The result gives Canada's rank (1 = highest) in the period most\nof them report. Bank of Canada Valet and StatCan are better for\nCanada's own latest figures.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"indicator":{"enum":["policy_rate","household_debt_service_ratio","private_debt_service_ratio","credit_to_gdp_gap","household_credit_to_gdp","private_credit_to_gdp","government_debt_to_gdp","real_house_price_growth","nominal_house_price_growth","real_house_price_index","cpi_inflation","real_effective_exchange_rate","nominal_effective_exchange_rate"],"type":"string"},"compare_with":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"start_period":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"end_period":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"last_n":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"lang":{"default":"en","enum":["en","fr"],"type":"string"}},"required":["indicator"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"boc_search_groups","description":"Search or list Bank of Canada Valet's series groups (~2,500).\n\nUse for: finding a themed group of related series (e.g. daily\nexchange rates, the CPI family including CPI-trim/median/common,\nweekly/monthly/annual commodity price indexes) when you want several\nrelated series at once rather than one series name. Pass `query`\nfor a keyword search (top `limit` matches, default 25, max 200). Omit\n`query` to page through the groups (`limit` default 50, max 1000).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"lang":{"default":"en","enum":["en","fr"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"boc_get_series","description":"Get the label, description and status of one Bank of Canada Valet series.\n\nUse for: confirming what a series code actually measures before\nrequesting its observations, e.g. FXUSDCAD (USD/CAD daily exchange\nrate), V39079 (target for the overnight rate / policy rate),\nV80691311 (prime rate), V41690973 (Total CPI). Also says whether it\nis still updated: `status` discontinued when its newest observation\n(`last_observation`) is far older than its frequency allows, with the\n`successor` where the Bank replaced it (the noon rate IEXE0101, last\n2017-04-28, by the daily average FXUSDCAD), and a `note` on FX* rates\n(indicative daily averages by about 16:30 ET, not transactional).","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"lang":{"default":"en","enum":["en","fr"],"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"boc_search_series","description":"Search or list Bank of Canada Valet's ~16,000 statistical series.\n\nUse for: finding a Valet series name when you only know a topic -\nexchange rates, interest rates (policy rate, prime rate), CPI/\ninflation measures, commodity prices, and hundreds of other\nmonetary/financial series. Pass `query` for a keyword search (top\n`limit` matches, default 25, max 200). Omit `query` to page through\nthe catalogue in name order (`limit` default 50, max 1000);\n`total_count` is the full number and provenance.limits says what was\ncut. Legacy series are listed too, each with `status`\n(active/discontinued, from its newest observation against its\nfrequency), `last_observation` and, where known, `successor`: e.g.\nthe noon rate IEXE0101 ended 2017-04-28, replaced by the daily\naverage FXUSDCAD. FX* rates carry a `note`: indicative daily\naverages published by about 16:30 ET, not transactional rates.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"lang":{"default":"en","enum":["en","fr"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"}}]}}}

